  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the antisemitic stereotype and historical scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material and visual material that together form the hateful joke. The text '*jew cooking time stops*' directly addresses the user by implying the user is part of the group being stereotyped (Jews) and that their 'cooking time' (a dehumanizing metaphor) is interrupted by the arrival of American forces. The user is also projected onto the scene of Nazi leaders at Auschwitz, which serves as the visual anchor for the joke, making the user feel implicated in the darkly humorous and offensive framing of the Holocaust. The meme does not use explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the projection is implicit through the user's identification with the target of the stereotype and the historical event being trivialized.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
